# Landing Page Guidelines

`documentation/src/components/landing/landing.tsx` composes the page. Each section lives in its own folder.

## Section Order (strict)

1. **Hero** (`hero/`): release badge, title, one line, agent skills command + Get Started, colour logo row,
   product video, HyperFlow download
2. **Clients** (`clients/`): eyebrow line, company logo carousel
3. **What is HyperFetch** (`what-is/`): "One framework, three parts", title left, Core / Sockets / DB tabs right,
   bento cards per tab
4. **Platforms** (`platforms/`): "Runs on every platform", technical card titles (Frontend, Native, Runtime,
   Realtime, Protocols, AI agents, TypeScript backends, Any backend, Tooling), logos only, no descriptions. Third-party
   logos with a dark mark use their `-dark` variant from `static/img`
5. **SDK** (`sdk/`): "Your backend, as a typed SDK", three story cards (Get your SDK, Plug in any protocol,
   Ship it), then the six features
6. **BetterTyped** (`bettertyped/`): "Built by BetterTyped" and the three numbers
7. **Hub** (`hub/`): "One typed client for every API", photon beam, live typed feed
8. **Production** (`production/`): "Ready for production" bento
9. **Persistence** (`persistence/`): "Everything is JSON", in two numbered parts. Each part is a pair of cards
   running three steps side by side. 01 Requests: Offline (queued, app closed, lost) and Persisted (queued, saved as
   JSON, synced). 02 Cache and DB: Cache (fetched, saved as JSON, instant reload) and DB (offline write, outbox as
   JSON, replayed). Then one `@hyper-fetch/db` strip (New) that links its docs. Keep it this simple: three icons per
   card, no extra cards
10. **Problems** (`problems/`): "Same bugs, different projects" issue tracker, loops
11. **Sponsors** (`sponsors/`)
12. **CallToAction** (`call-to-action/`): standard head, the hero actions, Apache 2.0 / stars / live downloads

## Hero Rules

- H1: "Fetch anything." / "Type everything.". "Fetch" uses the section-title zinc-200 gradient that fades at the top
  and bottom of each word, "anything." the BetterTyped gold (`bt-gold-text`). The whole second line uses the same
  fading gradient in zinc-300, one shade grayer. Only the squiggle under "everything." is red (`#f43f5e`)
- The Get Started button stays solid honey `#f9b233`, no gradient.
- Actions: the agent skills install command (click to copy) on the left, Get Started as the primary on the right.
- Logo row: colour logos with names, no label and no divider. Logos live in `static/img/integration-*.svg`.
  Add one when a new adapter, transport or integration page ships (`hero/ecosystem.tsx`).
- Under the video: one line of text, then "Download for {platform}" (direct installer from the HyperFlow
  release data) and "Other platforms".
- Background: the request paths at half strength, dots without labels. No particles.

## Style Rules

- Every section head uses `SectionHeader` from `shared/section-header.tsx`: optional eyebrow, title, optional
  one-line description, fixed spacing. Pass `align="left"` or `className="mb-0"` instead of custom heads.
- Eyebrows use the yellow-orange gradient, titles the zinc gradient (`SectionTitle`).
- Cards use `BentoCard` / `BentoGrid` from `shared/bento-card.tsx`: solid `#1f1f21`, the Highlighter spotlight on
  the edge, raised `#2a2a2d` elements inside. No left borders, no translucent cards.
- Little text: short titles, one line per card, concrete gains. No "Learn more" links inside cards.
- Wrap sections that size their own text in `.landing-scope` (resets the global 17px rule from `custom.css`).
- Use `motion` from `motion/react` for animations. Entrance reveals run once; illustrations may loop while on screen.
- Never mention `@hyper-fetch/testing`.

## Formatting Rules

- NEVER use em dashes (`—`) anywhere in landing page copy. Use a regular dash (`-`) or rewrite the sentence instead.
